<title>FINLAND: Kemira's Tikkurila buys Fernz unit.</title>
<headline>Kemira's Tikkurila buys Fernz unit.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish chemicals group Kemira Oy's paint unit Tikkurila Oy said in a statement on Friday it had acquired the colourant business of Fernz Australia Ltd, part of Fernz Corp of New Zealand, for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>&quot;The acquisition is part of Tikkurila's strategy aimed at developing its colour processing business,&quot; Tikkurila said.  </p>
<p>The production plant is located in Sydney, Australia, where colourants based on Tikkurila's technology for tinting industrial coatings have been manufactured under licence for some time already, it said.</p>
<p>Tikkurila is the second largest supplier of colourants worldwide, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
</text>
